promptMessages.content:
You are grading a model response for a routing capability benchmark.
Return JSON only with keys: score (number 0 to 1), rationale (string). No markdown fences.
Score 1.0 = fully meets expected response and grading criteria.
Score 0.0 = completely wrong or refusal without attempt.
Ignore chain-of-thought or reasoning preambles. Grade ONLY the extracted formatted deliverable.
For code-fix cases, verify the fix is correct — unchanged buggy code must score 0.
Placeholder diffs (----/+++), patches missing ---/+++ headers or any @@ hunk marker, malformed Codex patch envelopes, and reasoning prose submitted as code score 0.
For apply_patch, accept either ---/+++ headers with an @@ hunk marker and real change lines, or a Codex patch envelope (*** Begin Patch / *** Update File / @@ / *** End Patch). Bare @@ without line numbers is acceptable.
Required API tool calls: read_file, validate_schema, apply_patch.
Actual structured tool calls from API: read_file, validate_schema, apply_patch.
Fake tool syntax in prose (e.g. TOOL_CALL name=...) does not count unless criteria explicitly allow it.

Case: t03-tools-agent-plan

## Original question
[user]
Decompose and execute an agent plan with milestones: inspect router decisions API, compare local vs remote latency profiles, validate schema for difficultyRouting, apply patch to router.ts, and recommend routing strategy improvements.

## Example expected answer
Coherent plan or summary addressing the tool-using task.
Tool calls: read_file, validate_schema, apply_patch with ---/+++ headers plus @@ hunk marker (line numbers optional) or Codex patch envelope
Required fields: plan, patch_summary, strategy_improvements
(exemplar quality: derived)

## Key deliverables (grade against this checklist)
[MUST] Attempts the requested tool workflow without refusing outright.
[MUST] Emit API tool calls: read_file, validate_schema, apply_patch
[MUST] Include JSON keys: plan, patch_summary, strategy_improvements
[SHOULD] Match clues: read|search|list|patch|tool|plan
[MUST] apply_patch must contain either ---/+++ headers plus an @@ hunk marker and real change content, or a valid Codex patch envelope with real content; line numbers are optional and bare @@ is acceptable

## MUST NOT
MUST NOT use diff placeholders (----/+++, [file header])
MUST NOT emit prose-only TOOL_CALL lines without API tool_calls
MUST NOT submit reasoning prose as the graded code deliverable
MUST NOT leave apply_patch arguments as placeholder or malformed patch content

## Answer format requirements
BENCHMARK DELIVERABLE RULES:
Step 1: emit the required API tool calls. Step 2: after tools, output ONLY a ```json fence: {"plan":["..."],"patch_summary":"...","strategy_improvements":["..."]}.
Schema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "plan",
    "patch_summary",
    "strategy_improvements"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "plan": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "minItems": 3
    },
    "patch_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 12
    },
    "strategy_improvements": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "minItems": 2
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Reasoning is allowed before the deliverable, but only the formatted deliverable is graded.

## Grading criteria (authoritative)
Attempts the requested tool workflow without refusing outright.

## Subject deliverable to grade
{
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "name": "read_file",
      "arguments": {
        "path": "router.ts"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "read_file",
      "arguments": {
        "path": "difficultyRouting.schema.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate_schema",
      "arguments": {
        "document": "{\"difficultyRouting\":{\"local\":{\"p50Ms\":42,\"p95Ms\":95},\"remote\":{\"p50Ms\":68,\"p95Ms\":140},\"decisionPolicy\":{\"prefer\":\"local\",\"fallback\":\"remote\",\"maxRemoteForEasy\":0.2,\"difficultyThresholds\":{\"easy\":0.3,\"medium\":0.7,\"hard\":1.0}}}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "apply_patch",
      "arguments": {
        "diff": "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: router.ts\n@@\n export function createRouter(config: RouterConfig): Router {\n+  const difficultyRouting = {\n+    local: { p50Ms: 42, p95Ms: 95 },\n+    remote: { p50Ms: 68, p95Ms: 140 },\n+    decisionPolicy: {\n+      prefer: \"local\",\n+      fallback: \"remote\",\n+      maxRemoteForEasy: 0.2,\n+      difficultyThresholds: { easy: 0.3, medium: 0.7, hard: 1.0 }\n+    }\n+  };\n   return new RouterImpl(config);\n }\n*** End Patch"
      }
    }
  ]
}
